From: Protector of Earth Recomp
Subject: [PATCH] VU1 interpreter: per-pair step shared with translated code

What it is for:
  Translated VU1 microcode (a game port's own build-time translation of
  its closed list of VU programs) must give exactly the interpreter's
  results: registers, flags, cycle counts, VU memory, GIF output.

The change:
  - The body of VU1Interpreter::run's loop is split into loopHead (budget
    and stop checks, pipeline commit, PC bounds) and execPair (one decoded
    instruction pair: hazards and stalls, upper/lower execution, delayed
    writes, branch and halt handling, one cycle). Both are forced inline
    and defined in the header; run calls them exactly as before.
  - A NativeResolver (static, set by the game; VU1 only) fills a table of
    one function per instruction pair of the current code memory. run asks
    it again when the code may have changed (new upload generation, other
    buffer, or no PS2Memory), and calls the table's function for a pair
    when there is one, the cached decode + execPair otherwise.
  - The decoded-instruction types (Pipeline, VfAccess, InstructionUsage,
    DecodedInstructionPair) and RunFrame/StepResult are public; the
    VU1NativeAccess shim gives translated code execPair and gives a
    translator the decoder.
  A translated pair's function is execPair with the pair decoded at build
  time as a constant; the decoding depends only on the pair's 64 bits, so
  it does what the interpreter would.
  Tested: ps2xTest 454/454; without a resolver the 40 captured VU1
  workloads of the Ben 10 port give the same checksums as before
  (tools/vu1_replay --sum); with the port's translated code too.

